WEBVTT

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:03.177
Now apply the same reasoning to e-commerce data.

00:00:03.177 --> 00:00:08.832
Device type is nominal. Membership tier is ordinal when the business defines a real rank.

00:00:08.832 --> 00:00:11.317
Session duration is a ratio measurement.

00:00:11.317 --> 00:00:13.392
Purchases are a ratio count.

00:00:13.392 --> 00:00:20.412
Weekday is interesting because it is often treated as a nominal or cyclical category rather than a simple

00:00:20.412 --> 00:00:22.022
ordinal variable.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:27.782
Revenue is a ratio-scale monetary amount, but its database storage should use exact arithmetic and document

00:00:27.782 --> 00:00:33.877
currency. Connect this idea to an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:39.102
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:39.102 --> 00:00:46.192
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:46.192 --> 00:00:51.772
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.772 --> 00:00:56.640
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
